# Authored on Windows, deployed on Linux: pin LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, a fresh clone on a machine whose core.autocrlf=true gets a CRLF
# working tree. A CRLF shell script then fails inside the container with
# "bash\r: No such file or directory", and a CRLF Caddyfile/token can behave
# oddly too. `eol=lf` fixes the working tree as well as the repository blob.
* text=auto eol=lf
